WEBVTT
Language: en

NOTE
Written for this repository; the sentences pair with lecture-60s.ko.srt.

STYLE
::cue { color: white }

cue-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500 position:10% align:start
The cell membrane controls what goes in and out.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
The phospholipid bilayer has water-loving heads
and water-avoiding tails.

cue-3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.500
Proteins are embedded in the bilayer or sit on its surface.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.000
<i>Diffusion</i> uses no energy &amp; follows the concentration gradient.

cue-5
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.500
Glucose enters through a carrier protein.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.500
The calcium pump moves calcium ions out of the cell.

cue-7
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.500
This process needs ATP.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Osmosis is water crossing a semipermeable membrane.

cue-9
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.000
If the inside is more concentrated, water flows in.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.000
When the calcium pump stops, calcium inside the cell rises.

cue-11
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.000
Active transport moves substances against the concentration gradient.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:46.000
Rare syllables should display unchanged on this screen too.

cue-13
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:50.000
A receptor binds a signal molecule.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:54.000
Binding passes the signal on inside the cell.

cue-15
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.500
This signal decides how the cell responds.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.000
That is all for today's lecture.

